<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC
  "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN"
  "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
  <overview>
    <p>ECB should not be used as a mode for encryption. With a fixed key, identical plaintext blocks always produce identical ciphertext blocks. This can expose sensitive information by revealing patterns in the plaintext.</p>
  </overview>

  <recommendation>
    <p>Use an authenticated encryption mode such as GCM where available. If CBC is used, generate a fresh, unpredictable initialization vector for each encryption and use a separate message authentication mechanism to protect ciphertext integrity.</p>
  </recommendation>

  <example>
    <p>The following example shows six cases of instantiating a cipher with different block modes. In the 'BAD' cases, the encryption mode is ECB, which reveals patterns in the plaintext. In the 'GOOD' cases, the encryption mode is CBC with a randomly generated initialization vector, avoiding this issue. Authentication of the ciphertext is not shown.</p>
    <sample src="ECBEncryption.swift" />
  </example>

  <references>
    <li>Wikipedia, block cipher modes of operation, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Block_cipher_mode_of_operation#Electronic_codebook_.28ECB.29">Electronic codebook (ECB)</a>.</li>
  </references>
</qhelp>
